      </div>
      <details class="beep-help" id="beepHelp">
        <summary>⌨️ How to play & shortcuts</summary>
        <p class="beep-param-note">Middle row <span dir="ltr"><kbd>A</kbd> … <kbd>'</kbd></span> for the white keys, the row above <span dir="ltr"><kbd>W</kbd> <kbd>E</kbd> <kbd>T</kbd> <kbd>Y</kbd> <kbd>U</kbd> <kbd>O</kbd> <kbd>P</kbd></span> for the black keys, <kbd>Z</kbd> / <kbd>X</kbd> to shift the octave, and hold <kbd>Shift</kbd> for the sustain pedal. It also works with a keyboard plugged into your phone, a real MIDI keyboard, or by touching the keys directly: press near the top of a key for a soft note and near the bottom for a strong one. Recording shortcuts: <kbd>R</kbd> start/stop, and <kbd>Space</kbd> play/stop after your first recording (the full list appears with it).</p>
        <p class="beep-param-note">🎬 The video stays on your device and is never uploaded. It follows the white line: move the line to see the frame, and press play or record while you watch. Put a “cut marker” (M) at every cut in the scene and clips and effects snap to it. Step frame by frame with the buttons or the , and . keys — then download the video with your music, or the separate stems for your editing software.</p>
