          <p class="beep-param-note">Click an empty spot to add a note; drag across empty space to select several notes (or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd> for all, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+click to add one to the selection). Drag any selected note to move them all, or its right edge to change the length. <kbd>Delete</kbd> deletes, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd>/<kbd>X</kbd>/<kbd>V</kbd>/<kbd>D</kbd> copy, cut, paste (at the white line) and duplicate, <span dir="ltr">← →</span> move by a grid step and <span dir="ltr">↑ ↓</span> by a semitone (with <kbd>Shift</kbd>: a bar / an octave). Double-click a note to delete it; clicking a note name plays it.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="beep-param-note" id="beepTimelineHint">🔲 To select several layers: drag across empty space, or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd> for all, or <kbd>Shift</kbd>+click — dragging any of them moves them all, and delete, copy, duplicate, mute and the arrows apply to the whole selection. ↔️↕️ Drag any layer freely: left and right in time (on the grid), and up and down between tracks (drop it below the last track to start a new one). Drag a layer's edge to shorten or lengthen it without cutting: nothing is deleted, and lengthening brings back what was hidden. To place the white line, click or drag on the ruler or any empty space; recording starts there and the selected clip is split there. Double-click a layer to edit its notes, and click a track number to open its mixer.</p>
