  <section class="sounds-pane" id="paneLearn" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="beep-quiz sounds-lesson">
      <p class="beep-params-title">🎚️ The four parameters of sound</p>
      <p class="beep-param-note">Every sound you hear can be described by four parameters: <strong>frequency</strong> (how high or low the pitch is), <strong>rhythm</strong> (note lengths and the speed of the pulse), <strong>timbre</strong> (the color that tells one instrument from another), and <strong>dynamics</strong> (loudness, marked p for soft and f for loud). Try changing each one on its own in the "Compose" tab.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="beep-quiz sounds-lesson">
      <p class="beep-params-title">💰 Note lengths are like money</p>
      <p class="beep-param-note">Whole note (hollow, no stem) = 4 dinars · half note (hollow with stem) = 2 · quarter note = 1 dinar · eighth note = 500 fils · sixteenth = 250 fils. A dot next to a note adds half its value (a dotted half = 3 dinars).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="beep-quiz sounds-lesson">
      <p class="beep-params-title">🎹 Major vs. minor chords</p>
      <p class="beep-param-note">The only difference is the middle note: 4 semitones above the root in a major chord, 3 in a minor one. That small gap is what makes major sound bright and minor sound sad.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="beep-quiz sounds-lesson piper" id="piperLesson">
      <p class="beep-params-title">🎬 Scoring exercise: the first 36 seconds of Piper</p>
      <p class="beep-param-note">An exercise from a music production course: score a short scene that moves through five emotional states, each with its own instruments and instruction. Press the button to hear an example that applies them, and watch the highlighted section follow the music.</p>
      <button type="button" class="btn secondary" id="piperPlay" data-play="▶️ Listen to the example" data-stop="⏹ Stop">▶️ Listen to the example</button>
      <div class="piper-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span id="piperProgress"></span></div>
      <ol class="piper-list" id="piperList">
        <li data-start="0" data-end="3"><span class="piper-time" dir="ltr">0:00–0:03</span><div><strong>Curiosity</strong><span class="piper-inst">Clarinet solo (motif)</span><small>Create a short, repeating motif using two or three notes.</small></div></li>
        <li data-start="3" data-end="8"><span class="piper-time" dir="ltr">0:03–0:08</span><div><strong>Tension</strong><span class="piper-inst">String ensemble + Beauty Blubbers</span><small>Add dissonance and gradually increase the volume using automation.</small></div></li>
        <li data-start="8" data-end="13"><span class="piper-time" dir="ltr">0:08–0:13</span><div><strong>Danger / Waves</strong><span class="piper-inst">String ensemble + Dusty Strings + Foley (waves)</span><small>Increase tension through dissonance and intensity.</small></div></li>
        <li data-start="13" data-end="23"><span class="piper-time" dir="ltr">0:13–0:23</span><div><strong>Time freezes</strong><span class="piper-inst">Event Horizon + Foley (bubbles)</span><small>Use static harmony and long sustained sounds, with little or no rhythm. Use reverb to create space.</small></div></li>
        <li data-start="23" data-end="36"><span class="piper-time" dir="ltr">0:23–0:36</span><div><strong>Uplifting / Happy</strong><span class="piper-inst">String ensemble + clarinet solo (motif) + marimba</span><small>Use consonant, major harmony and gradually increase the energy.</small></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="beep-params-title">Technical</p>
      <ul class="piper-tech">
        <li><strong>Automation:</strong> volume and panning.</li>
        <li><strong>Tempo:</strong> use the Tempo Track when appropriate.</li>
        <li><strong>Plugins:</strong> EQ + reverb (Space Designer) on each layer.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="beep-param-note">🎧 The example is generated in code to apply the instructions; it is not the film's original score. Beauty Blubbers and Event Horizon are sounds from the course library, so they are stood in for by a celesta shimmer and a long choir chord.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="beep-quiz" id="beepQuiz" data-right="✅ Correct! It was: " data-wrong="❌ Not quite — it was: " data-names="Frequency|Rhythm|Timbre|Dynamics">
      <p class="beep-params-title">👂 Ear training: what changed?</p>
      <p class="beep-param-note">You'll hear the same clip twice; the second time, exactly one parameter changes. Guess which.</p>
      <button type="button" class="btn secondary" id="beepQuizPlay">▶️ Hear both clips</button>
      <div class="instrument-picker">
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip quiz-btn" data-answer="pitch" disabled>Frequency</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip quiz-btn" data-answer="rhythm" disabled>Rhythm</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip quiz-btn" data-answer="timbre" disabled>Timbre</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip quiz-btn" data-answer="dynamics" disabled>Dynamics</button>
      </div>
      <p class="beep-quiz-result" id="beepQuizResult" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
    <p class="beep-experiment-hint">📚 The learning tools here are inspired by a music production course the site's owner is taking at university.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sounds-pane" id="panePractice" role="tabpanel" hidden data-drop="⬇️ Drop the file here">
    <div class="beep-play song-practice" id="songPractice" data-groups="Low 3|Low 2|Low|Middle|High|High 2|High 3" data-saved="✅ Saved in your browser" data-del-ask="Delete this song from your browser?" data-bad="Could not read the file" data-loaded="✅ Song opened" data-empty="Type some notes first" data-wait="Press the glowing key" data-done="🎉 Finished! Mistakes: " data-full="Browser storage is full — use “Download file” to keep it" data-notes=" notes">
      <div class="song-lib">
        <select id="songList" aria-label="Your songs"><option value="">— New song —</option></select>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songSave">💾 Save</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songDownload">⬇️ Download file</button>
        <label class="filter-chip" for="songFile">📂 Open file</label>
        <input type="file" id="songFile" hidden />
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songDelete" aria-label="Delete song" title="Delete song">🗑️</button>
      </div>
      <details class="beep-help song-editor" id="songEditor" open>
        <summary>✍️ Type or paste the notes</summary>
        <input type="text" id="songTitle" class="instrument-search" placeholder="Song title" aria-label="Song title" />
        <textarea id="songText" class="song-text" dir="ltr" rows="7" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Example:
E E F G G F E D
C C D E E-D D

Or paste letter notes from a site like noobnotes" aria-label="✍️ Type or paste the notes"></textarea>
        <div class="song-write" id="songWrite">
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songWriteToggle" aria-pressed="false" title="Press piano keys and the notes are written for you, in the right group">✍️ Write with the piano</button>
          <div class="instrument-picker" id="songWriteLen" role="group" aria-label="Length">
            <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-len="0.5">Short</button>
            <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-len="1">Normal</button>
            <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-len="2">Long</button>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songWriteChord" aria-pressed="false" title="Keys you press next are written together (played at the same time)">🎹 Chord</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songWriteRest">⏸ Rest</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songWriteLine">↵ Line</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songWriteBack" aria-label="Delete the last note" title="Delete the last note">⌫</button>
        </div>
        <div class="song-chips" id="songChips" role="group" aria-label="Written notes — tap any to hear it"></div>
        <p class="beep-param-note song-groups-hint">🎨 Each key’s color = its group: “Middle” is green, “Low” blue, “High” yellow. When typing letters: <span dir="ltr">^</span> = high, <span dir="ltr">.</span> = low.</p>
        <p class="beep-param-note">Each note is a letter: <span dir="ltr">C D E F G A B</span> (or Do Re Mi), with <span dir="ltr">#</span> or <span dir="ltr">b</span> after it for sharp and flat. <span dir="ltr">^</span> before it = one octave up, <span dir="ltr">.</span> before it = one down. Every note is an even half beat, <span dir="ltr">~</span> holds the previous note longer, and <span dir="ltr">_</span> is a rest. To press several keys together: <span dir="ltr">C+E+G</span> or <span dir="ltr">[C E G]</span>; for an exact length: <span dir="ltr">C:2</span>. Lyric lines are skipped when playing and shown above the piano.</p>
        <p class="beep-param-note">🎼 For musicians: paste a piece in <bdi dir="ltr">ABC</bdi> notation (with a <span dir="ltr">K:</span> line) and it is read with its meter, key and note values, or open a MIDI or MusicXML file (from MuseScore and others: each hand is a track).</p>
      </details>
      <div class="song-tracks" id="songTracks" data-families="Piano|Chromatic percussion|Organ|Guitar|Bass|Strings|Ensemble|Brass|Reed|Pipe|Synth lead|Synth pad|Synth effects|Ethnic|Percussive|Sound effects" data-track="Track" hidden>
        <p class="beep-setting-label">🎼 MIDI file — choose the tracks to practice:</p>
        <div class="instrument-picker" id="songTrackChips"></div>
        <div class="instrument-picker" id="songHands" role="group" aria-label="Hand">
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-hand="both">🙌 Both hands</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-hand="right">🫱 Right hand</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-hand="left">🫲 Left hand</button>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songToText">✍️ Type notes instead</button>
      </div>
      <div class="song-controls">
        <button type="button" class="btn" id="songListen" data-stop="⏸ Pause">▶️ Listen</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn secondary" id="songTrain" data-stop="⏸ Pause">🎯 Practice</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songStaffToggle" aria-pressed="false" title="Show the piece on the staff (treble and bass clef); the next note lights up">🎼 Sheet music</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songSimple" aria-pressed="false" title="Folds every note of the song into two octaves: bigger, easier keys, same melody in a closer octave">🎹 Simplify keyboard</button>
        <div class="instrument-picker" id="songSpeed" role="group" aria-label="Speed">
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-speed="0.5">🐢 50%</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-speed="0.75">75%</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip active" data-speed="1">100%</button>
          <button type="button" class="filter-chip" data-speed="1.25">125%</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="song-status" id="songStatus" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="song-lyric" id="songLyric" dir="auto"></p>
      <div class="beep-staff-scroll song-staff" id="songStaff" hidden></div>
      <div class="song-timeline" id="songTimeline" dir="ltr" hidden>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songRestart" aria-label="From the start" title="From the start (Home)">⏮</button>
        <span id="songTimeNow">0:00</span>
        <input type="range" id="songSeek" min="0" max="1000" step="1" value="0" aria-label="Song position" />
        <span id="songTimeAll">0:00</span>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="songLoop" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Loop a passage, bar to bar" title="Loop a passage, bar to bar">🔁</button>
        <span class="song-loop" id="songLoopRange" dir="ltr" hidden><label>From bar <input type="number" id="songLoopFrom" min="1" value="1" inputmode="numeric" /></label> <label>to <input type="number" id="songLoopTo" min="1" value="4" inputmode="numeric" /></label></span>
      </div>
      <div class="song-keys-slot" id="songKeysSlot"></div>
      <p class="beep-param-note">Practice mode waits for you: the bars fall and stop at the line until you press the right note — by touch, computer keyboard, or a MIDI keyboard. You can also open a MIDI file (from sites like bitmidi.com) and it falls with its exact rhythm. Keyboard: <kbd>Space</kbd> play/pause, <kbd>Home</kbd> back to the start.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
